  "purpose": "MyGardener plant research contract: consumer relevance, calendar event semantics, regional pest relevance, Thrive and monitoring inputs.",
  "principles": [
    "Store biological response thresholds separately from geographic zone labels.",
    "Do not infer precipitation requirements from irrigation demand.",
    "Every active Thrive module carries its own confidence and evidence basis.",
    "Missing evidence remains missing; inferred fallbacks must be marked and cannot create T5 Core.",
    "Seasonal/protected suitability is orthogonal to T1-T5 year-round outdoor suitability.",
    "A management option does not imply management is required; intervention changes class only when the climate constraint needs it.",
    "Survival and phenological/production success are distinct outputs.",
    "Calendar thermal-time values are event-specific and remain null when no defensible GDD/chill literature exists; static local calendar windows remain fallback priors.",
    "Reference ET coefficients are optional; absence must fall back to conservative category/drought-tolerance estimates rather than fabricated precision."
